Q: Change height of iframe dynamically on tab change? A: <p>Assuming you are using bootstrap...</p>

<p>One problem with this code is that you did not wrap your columns in a .row. it should be written like this: </p>

<pre><code>&lt;div class="container"&gt;
&lt;div class="row"&gt;
&lt;div class="col-sm-12"&gt;
[content]
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Another potential issue with the code could be the class ".in" that you gave the first iframe's parent div but did not give it to the rest. Most likely the only difference in all of those parent divs should be the one instance where you have the class ".active"</p>

Q: To Grey Out the WHOLE web site when you click button inside Iframe contained in that web site A: <p>I think setting the grey to when the iframe window has focus may work for you. </p>

<p>You didn't include any code so not sure if you're using jQuery, but try something like this.</p>

<pre>
while($(iframe).focus()){
   $('document').addClass('grey-out');
}
</pre>

Q: Is there a way to call just a certain part of a web site into an iframe? A: <p>If you dont mind calling the whole page you can manipulate a DIV to make it LOOK like this is happening.  The following code worked for me:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div style="overflow:hidden; width:608px; height:270px;"&gt;
  &lt;iframe  scrolling="no" frameBorder="0"
  src="http://tech-revolution.com/forum/vbshout.php?do=detach&amp;instanceid=1#dbtech_shoutbox1" 
  style="width:728px; height:270px; border:none; margin-left:-60px;"/&gt;  
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>But perhaps you should check with that component's authors to see if there's a way to render it the way you want on their server and you'll just need to frame a different URL.</p>
